        "id": 5707
      },
      "writtenOn": "2014-02-12T23:14:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So I agree it does not strictly need it.  I was thinking of the issues of:\n1) If we make role-assignment a first class entity at some point (as we discussed) this would be needed\n\n2) For people (like Rackspace and others) who running multi-Active DB replication between keystones in different regions….is it better (from a recovery point of view) in the case when two sites both added the \"same\" entry, to allow the benign result of two entries (since they would have different IDs) vs a sync clash that needs to be handled?  However, I think the UniqueConstraint would also trigger this, so not sure I achieved my goal anyway!\n\nHaving said all that, I think I\u0027m actually i favour of removing the ID for now.",
